WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:10.617
Roadmaps lay out what’s coming over the next months on one timeline: store openings, menu launches, app releases. In this video, you’ll read a roadmap and change it.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:19.935
Open Roadmaps to see your company’s roadmaps. A roadmap can be shared with everyone, or kept private to you, like this build-out schedule.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:28.741
Open one. Each lane is a line of work, like stores, the menu, or the app, with a bar for each piece of work from its start to its end.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.597
Choose how much time to show, from one week to two years. Six months fits this plan nicely.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:42.095
The fill shows how far along each one is, and markers flag the dates that matter, like the day Bayview opens its doors.

00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:50.981
Click Edit roadmap to add lanes, bars and markers. Drag a bar to move it, or its edge to change its dates, and it saves as you go.

00:00:51.433 --> 00:01:01.673
New lane adds a line of work. New bar adds a piece of work to a lane, with its dates, color and progress. New marker pins a date, for the whole roadmap or one lane.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:08.661
Visibility decides who sees it: everyone in the company, or just you. Make private hides it while you work on it.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:15.713
Roadmaps sit alongside Projects and Product Releases, so the big picture and the day-to-day work stay in one place.

